1
00:00:00,150 --> 00:00:05,700
Real Madrid fans… standing up to applaud a Barcelona player. In their own stadium.

2
00:00:05,750 --> 00:00:12,000
November 19, 2005. The Clásico, at the Bernabéu.

3
00:00:12,050 --> 00:00:14,400
Barcelona were already 1–0 up.

4
00:00:14,450 --> 00:00:19,000
Then Ronaldinho picked up the ball on the left… ran at Sergio Ramos…

5
00:00:19,050 --> 00:00:24,100
…went past him… and fired it in. 2–0.

6
00:00:24,150 --> 00:00:30,600
18 minutes later, he did it again. Past Ramos… and low, under Iker Casillas.

7
00:00:30,650 --> 00:00:33,300
3–0.

8
00:00:33,350 --> 00:00:40,200
And then something strange happened. Thousands of Madrid fans rose to their feet… and clapped.

9
00:00:40,250 --> 00:00:47,800
Before him, the only Barcelona player said to get that honour was Diego Maradona, in 1983.

10
00:00:47,850 --> 00:00:51,650
Nine days later, Ronaldinho won the Ballon d’Or.

11
00:00:51,700 --> 00:00:56,400
Would your fans ever clap for a rival? Tell me in the comments.
